  "id": "COMPOUND:42695 - PROTEIN:5832",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between 5,8-Dihydroxy-2-(2-phenylethyl)chromone and HuT78 through a series of molecular targets. The compound is linked to CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is a target of multiple compounds, including 2,4-Bis[(4-hydroxyphenyl)methyl]-5-methoxy-3-[2-(3-methoxyphenyl)ethyl]phenol and 2-Methylheptyl propanoate. All these targets ultimately have HuT78 as their target. This indicates that the compound may act through a common pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of sialyltransferases, which are involved in the synthesis of sialic acid. The evidence suggests that the compound may influence HuT78 through a mechanism involving sialyltransferase activity, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
